## Feedback loop

Write a session summary into `interactions/sessions/` on `!save` or when the
user explicitly asks to save. Do not invent a write because "enough material
has accumulated".

### Commands

| Command | What it does | Cost |
|---------|--------------|------|
| `!view` | Start or reopen the local read-only knowledge graph viewer | 0 tokens |
| `!save` | Save session summary + enrichment now | ~2K tokens |
| `!reflect` | Run reflection: synthesize insights from accumulated facts | ~15K tokens |
| `!audit` | Level-2 review in a **new session** per pack: open `.repomix/audit/<pack>__request.md`. Finding without `file:line` + quote is dropped. Cross-pack pass: `CROSS_PACK__request.md` (titles only). | ~5–20K per pack |
| `!review` | Walk through `review/needs-classification/`, `review/needs-ai-decision/`, `review/needs-redaction/` and process every item: extract durable knowledge into `knowledge/`, redact sensitive material, archive what cannot be used. Explain per item what came in, what you extracted, and where it landed. If you cannot decide without input, ask one specific question per item. Honor long-form-book hints (write takeaways, do not copy prose into `voice/`). | ~5–30K tokens |
| `!populate` | Regenerate `DATA_PLACEMENT_EXAMPLES.md` (run `python3 scripts/kb_populate.py --role <role> --kb-root .`) | ~50 tokens |
| `!export` | Pack this base into a bundle for another machine (run `python3 scripts/kb_export.py`) and tell the user where the file landed | ~100 tokens |
| `!import` | Merge bundles waiting in `sync/inbox/` (run `python3 scripts/kb_import.py`), then summarize the report | ~200 tokens |
| `!merge` | Finish an import: resolve every package in `review/needs-merge/`, audit the merged pages for contradictions, cross-link the new knowledge, refresh routing, lint and reindex. Full procedure in `16_MERGE.md`. | ~5–40K tokens |
| `!heal` | Catch up an upgraded base: run `python3 scripts/kb_heal.py --plan`, apply auto, walk assisted items one by one. Procedure in `18_HEAL.md`. Stage 4 (trim) is locked until eval questions exist. | ~0–40K tokens |
| `!refactor` | Two-step instruction trim: audit `AGENTS.md` (and listed base files), stop for owner decisions, then rewrite from those decisions only. Procedure in `17_REFACTOR.md`. Backup first. `--global` reports conflicts with `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` and writes nothing. | ~5–40K tokens |
| `!profile-review` | Read `knowledge/profile/`. Ask what is missing (3 questions at a time, important first); then what may be stale. Update pages from answers. Stamp `profile_review.reviewed_at`. | ~5–15K tokens |
| `!quiz` | Five questions about what is already in the base; costliest mistakes first. Answers → `interactions/quiz/`. | ~5–15K tokens |
| `!super` | Toggle mode: default ↔ super | 0 tokens |
| `!super on/off` | Explicitly enable/disable super mode | 0 tokens |
| `!super status` | Show current mode | 0 tokens |

Graph, sync, and heal are the scripts in the table — do not rebuild the
graph or invent export/import/merge mechanics with AI.

## Knowledge lifecycle

- `knowledge/decisions/` — immutable (log style, do not edit historical entries)
- `knowledge/domain/` — update when the underlying data changes
- `knowledge/playbooks/` — update when processes change
- `knowledge/insights/` — synthesis from facts; update when new data arrives
- `knowledge/profile/` — update on professional/career changes
- Outdated knowledge → `knowledge/_archive/` with a note
- Frontmatter `last_verified` — refresh on confirmed accuracy

## Operating mode

At the start of each session, **read `mode` in `kb.config.yml`** and apply the corresponding profile from `mode_profiles`.

| Mode | Paradigm | Tokens/day | Use when |
|------|----------|-----------:|----------|
| `default` | Python-first, throttled | ~3-4K | Daily work, limited budget |
| `super` | AI-first, on-demand | ~50-200K+ | Unlimited plans, intensive learning |

> ⚠️ **Super mode** can drain a daily token budget in one active session. Use only with unlimited or high-cap AI plans.

## Context budget

1. Reading priority: insights → opinions → domain → playbooks → raw facts
2. Routing first: always start with the routing table; don't load every domain file
3. Loading limit: at most 7 `knowledge/` files in context simultaneously
4. Summarize what you've read before loading more
5. Ranking: prefer files with high `importance` and recent `last_accessed`
6. Temporal filter: filter by `valid_from`/`valid_until` if the question is period-specific
7. Access tracking: update `last_accessed` and `access_count += 1` only when the page actually influenced the answer — not on every glance

